id: pm-ts-starter-rku9
title: Consume canonical launcher non-ENOENT diagnostic repair after pm-ops publication
description: "Cubic PR #114 finding reproduced in a disposable project: NODE_PATH points at a regular file, installer resolution fails, lstat presence probing raises ENOTDIR and masks the original MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Installation still fails closed and never prints the omit-dev skip. Keep consumer byte-identical to pinned pm-ops template. Canonical repair must preserve original resolution errors for non-ENOENT stat failures, receive tests and publication in pm-ops, then update this consumer pin/template and rerun acceptance."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-02T22:50:31.100Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T22:57:16.747Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Canonical published pm-ops launcher treats non-ENOENT probe failures as absence not proven and rethrows original resolution error. Consumer remains byte-identical to published template. Real NODE_PATH file and permission fixtures pass without an omit-dev skip.
repro_steps: "Create a disposable empty package with type=module. Copy scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts into it unchanged. Create a regular file named not-a-directory and execute the copy from that empty package with NODE_PATH set to that file. Current canonical launcher exits nonzero with ENOTDIR instead of the original MODULE_NOT_FOUND and does not emit the omit-dev skip notice. Remove the fixture afterward. This is a diagnostic reproduction, not an accepted masking regression or a durable linked test."
body: ""
